/*!
@class dCsvData_c
@details
## Overview
This class reads the CSV files located in WorldMap/RouteInfo.arc, which describe the structure of the world map -
how the nodes are connected, which course unlocks which other course, and which world map enemies are present.

## Point data layout
Each line in the point CSV file contains a number of fields, separated by commas.
If no more non-empty fields are present, the line may be terminated early with a carriage return and newline character.

The fields are as follows:
### Line number
This is ignored by the game but is just a sequential number starting from 1 for each line in the file.
### Point name
The name of the point which is being described.
### Point types
This is a comma-separated list of properties of the point. See PointFlag_e.
### Open point names (Regular exit)
This is a comma-separated list of point names which are unlocked when the player completes the course at this point.
### Open route names (Regular exit)
This is a comma-separated list of route names which are unlocked when the player completes the course at this point.
### Flag data (Regular exit)
This seems to never be used in the vanilla world maps, but it is referenced in:
- ReadFlagData()
- GetRouteAnimNum()
- GetRouteAnimName()
### Open point names (Secret exit)
This is a comma-separated list of point names which are unlocked when the player completes the secret exit of the course at this point.
### Open route names (Secret exit)
This is a comma-separated list of route names which are unlocked when the player completes the secret exit of the course at this point.
### Flag data (Secret exit)
See the regular exit version of this.

## Route data layout
Each line in the route CSV file contains a number of fields, separated by commas.
The fields are as follows:
### Route name
The name of the route, in the format @p Rxxxxyyyy, where @p xxxx and @p yyyy denote the two connected points.
### Route action type
The type of the route. This determines the animation of the player when they traverse the route. See ActionType_e.
### Route Flags
This is a comma-separated list of flags for the route. Only used in World 5 for the moving vines.

*/
